course: dictionary
lesson: 5073
title: Instruct: tell, teach, or hire
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Read the words around «instruct» and ask: who is doing the telling, and what happens next?
explain: «They instructed his housekeeper to feed him, undress him, and put him to bed.» The list of jobs that follows is the clue. Instruct means they told her exactly what to do, especially with authority.
explain: The same word can also mean to teach a skill, or, in UK law, to hire a lawyer. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «They told his housekeeper to feed him» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: «Instruct» means to tell someone what they must do, especially officially or with authority.
fact: «Instruct» can also mean to teach someone a skill, such as «instruct someone in swimming».
fact: In UK law, «instruct» means to hire a lawyer to work for you.
fact: «As instructed» means in the way you were told.
fact: Instructions are the steps you must follow, like the steps in a maths question.
exercise: «The sign instructed visitors to keep off the grass.» What does instructed mean here? | Made them laugh | *Told them what they must do | Hired them to work in the park | Taught them to play football
exercise: Mia's dad will instruct her in swimming at the pool. What does instruct mean here? | Tell her to stop | Shout at her | *Teach her a skill | Hire a lawyer for her
exercise: Maths instructions tell you the steps to follow. What does «as instructed» mean? | As fast as you can | In a different way from the book | *In the way you were told | Without any help at all
test: In UK law, to instruct a lawyer means to: | Read their letter aloud | Teach them to swim | *Hire them to work for you | Argue with a judge
test: Which sentence uses instruct to mean teach? | The rain will instruct the football team | The teacher was instructed to go home | The sign will instruct everyone to leave | *Dad will instruct me in chess on Sunday
exam: Read «They instructed his housekeeper to feed him, undress him, and put him to bed.» Which meaning fits best, and why? | Hired her to work in a shop | Asked her to find a lost dog | Taught her how to cook a meal | *Told her what she must do, because feeding, undressing and bedtime are the jobs she was given
